WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:20.982
Darkness seemed to swim around me as I sat at a table in my room, resting my head

2
00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:21.722
on my arms.

3
00:00:22.923 --> 00:00:26.025
Mr. Rochester was not what I had thought him to be.

4
00:00:27.246 --> 00:00:30.708
I knew I must leave him, but I had no strength to flee.

5
00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.005
Late in the afternoon I raised my head.

6
00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:36.025
"What am I to do?"

7
00:00:36.425 --> 00:00:37.266
I asked myself.

8
00:00:38.366 --> 00:00:44.227
But the answer that came to mind—leave Thornfield—was so dreadful that I couldn't bear it.

9
00:00:45.388 --> 00:00:46.888
I stood up and my head spun.

10
00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:51.109
Then I remembered that I hadn't eaten anything since breakfast.

11
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.650
I opened my door and stumbled over Mr.

12
00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.771
Rochester, who was sitting in a chair at my threshold.

13
00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:01.756
"You shut yourself up and grieve alone," he said.

14
00:01:01.776 --> 00:01:05.138
"I would prefer you come out and shout at me."

15
00:01:06.279 --> 00:01:08.540
I said nothing but regarded him wearily.

16
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.502
"Jane, I never meant to wound you.

17
00:01:13.623 --> 00:01:14.764
Will you ever forgive me?"

18
00:01:15.904 --> 00:01:17.925
Reader, I forgave him on the spot.

19
00:01:19.006 --> 00:01:24.689
There was such deep remorse in his eye, such pity in his voice, and such unchanged love in

20
00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:25.310
his manner.

21
00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.332
I forgave him all but did not tell him so.

22
00:01:30.452 --> 00:01:32.053
"You know I'm a scoundrel, Jane?"

23
00:01:32.414 --> 00:01:33.134
he inquired.

24
00:01:34.335 --> 00:01:36.657
I suppose he wondered at my continued silence.

25
00:01:37.898 --> 00:01:38.459
"Yes, sir."

26
00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:40.380
"Then tell me that."

27
00:01:41.421 --> 00:01:41.981
"I cannot.

28
00:01:42.982 --> 00:01:45.124
I am sick and tired, and I want some water."

29
00:01:46.225 --> 00:01:51.909
He heaved a shuddering sigh, and taking me in his arms, carried me downstairs to the library.

30
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.792
There he brought me a glass of water.

31
00:01:55.984 --> 00:02:01.107
Then suddenly overcome with passion, he tried to kiss me, but I turned my face away.

32
00:02:01.127 --> 00:02:03.569
"What's this?"

33
00:02:04.029 --> 00:02:04.749
he exclaimed.

34
00:02:04.769 --> 00:02:07.991
"You won't kiss the husband of Bertha Mason.

35
00:02:09.192 --> 00:02:09.772
Is that right?

36
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:12.674
You consider my arms already filled?"

37
00:02:12.694 --> 00:02:15.476
"At any rate there is no room for me."

38
00:02:15.496 --> 00:02:19.518
"So you intend to live under this roof only as Adele's governess?"

39
00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:22.480
"Adele must have a new governess, sir."

40
00:02:23.572 --> 00:02:27.735
"I have already settled that Adele will go to school, and I don't mean to torment you with

41
00:02:27.775 --> 00:02:29.856
hideous recollections of this accursed place.

42
00:02:31.137 --> 00:02:32.078
We won't stay here.

43
00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:37.822
I'll give Grace Poole two hundred pounds a year to live here with my wife, as you term

44
00:02:37.842 --> 00:02:43.186
that fearful hag who burns people in their beds and—" "Sir," I interrupted.

45
00:02:43.206 --> 00:02:47.749
"You speak of her with such hate, but she cannot help being insane."

46
00:02:47.769 --> 00:02:52.372
"Jane, my darling, it's not because she's insane that I hate her.

47
00:02:54.248 --> 00:02:56.310
If you were insane, do you think I would hate you?"

48
00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.271
"I do indeed."

49
00:02:58.291 --> 00:03:02.735
"Then you know nothing about the sort of love that I am capable of."

50
00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:08.139
I had been struggling with tears because I knew he wouldn't like to see me weep, but now

51
00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:09.761
I let my tears flow freely.

52
00:03:10.962 --> 00:03:13.824
He tried to pull me to him, but I would have none of that.

53
00:03:13.844 --> 00:03:16.066
"You don't love me then?"

54
00:03:16.486 --> 00:03:17.327
he said bitterly.

55
00:03:17.347 --> 00:03:20.690
"It was only your status as my wife that you valued?"

56
00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:23.452
"I do love you," I said.

57
00:03:24.648 --> 00:03:25.528
"More than ever.

58
00:03:26.669 --> 00:03:29.970
But this is the last time I must say that, and I must leave you."

59
00:03:31.171 --> 00:03:31.651
"Leave me?

60
00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.612
No, no, Jane.

61
00:03:33.932 --> 00:03:37.433
I only ask you to endure one more night under this roof, and then we will go to

62
00:03:37.474 --> 00:03:39.094
a villa I have in the south of France.

63
00:03:40.255 --> 00:03:42.436
You shall be my wife as if I were not married."

64
00:03:44.296 --> 00:03:45.077
I shook my head.

65
00:03:45.097 --> 00:03:48.638
"If I lived with you like that, I would be your mistress."

66
00:03:48.658 --> 00:03:50.979
"What a fool I am!"

67
00:03:51.339 --> 00:03:52.500
Mr. Rochester cried.

68
00:03:53.788 --> 00:03:58.111
"I keep saying that I'm not married, but I forget that you know nothing of that infernal woman

69
00:03:58.291 --> 00:04:00.032
or the circumstances of our union."

70
00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:03.834
He began by telling me what I'd already heard from Mrs.

71
00:04:03.874 --> 00:04:09.938
Fairfax—that his father didn't want him to be poor when Rowland, his older brother, inherited everything.

72
00:04:11.179 --> 00:04:17.002
Then Rochester said that his father and Rowland arranged for him to marry Bertha Mason, who had a

73
00:04:17.063 --> 00:04:19.084
dowry of thirty thousand pounds.

74
00:04:20.384 --> 00:04:23.725
He went to Jamaica and was dazzled by the beautiful Bertha.

75
00:04:23.745 --> 00:04:29.648
"I seldom saw her alone, but every man seemed to admire her and envy me.

76
00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:33.590
A marriage took place almost before I knew where I was.

77
00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:35.751
I never loved her.

78
00:04:35.871 --> 00:04:36.971
I didn't even know her!"

79
00:04:38.872 --> 00:04:40.773
He thought his wife's mother was dead.

80
00:04:42.053 --> 00:04:47.255
Only after the wedding did he learn that she was shut up in an insane asylum, as was

81
00:04:47.315 --> 00:04:48.396
Bertha's younger brother.

82
00:04:49.716 --> 00:04:53.559
"My father and Rowland knew all this but thought only of Bertha's dowry.

83
00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.602
I lived with her for four years.

84
00:04:57.923 --> 00:05:03.007
I will spare you the abominable details except to say that no servant would stay because of the

85
00:05:03.047 --> 00:05:08.651
continued outbreaks of her violent temper, and I couldn't divorce her because the doctors had discovered that she

86
00:05:08.691 --> 00:05:09.412
was insane."

87
00:05:09.432 --> 00:05:13.375
"I sincerely pity you, sir," I said quietly.

88
00:05:13.395 --> 00:05:14.836
"Go on."

89
00:05:16.064 --> 00:05:17.826
One night in Jamaica, Mr.

90
00:05:17.886 --> 00:05:22.910
Rochester decided to flee to Europe, where he could live without anyone knowing his past.

91
00:05:24.111 --> 00:05:28.375
He brought Bertha back to Thornfield and left her in the care of Grace Poole.

92
00:05:30.217 --> 00:05:33.179
For ten years he roamed from one country to another.

93
00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.384
He had three mistresses, including Adele's mother, Celine Varens.

94
00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:43.168
"I now hate to remember the time I spent with those women," he said.

95
00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:49.764
I felt the truth of those words and knew if I became his next mistress, he would one

96
00:05:49.804 --> 00:05:51.405
day regard me the same way.

97
00:05:51.425 --> 00:05:58.370
"I was searching for love," he said, "but never found it until one day when I was returning

98
00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.711
to Thornfield on business.

99
00:06:01.032 --> 00:06:07.797
My horse slipped on some ice—" "Don't talk to me of those days, sir," I interrupted, wiping tears

100
00:06:07.857 --> 00:06:08.537
from my eyes.

101
00:06:08.557 --> 00:06:12.180
"All I ask, Jane, is that you promise to be mine."

102
00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.881
"Mr. Rochester, I will not be yours."

103
00:06:17.081 --> 00:06:18.121
I rose from my chair.

104
00:06:18.141 --> 00:06:20.562
"Oh, Jane!

105
00:06:21.622 --> 00:06:23.423
My hope, my love, my life!"

106
00:06:24.643 --> 00:06:27.804
He cried out in anguish and a sob escaped his lips.

107
00:06:29.005 --> 00:06:30.805
I kissed his cheek and fled the room.

108
00:06:32.005 --> 00:06:34.746
The next morning I slipped quietly from Thornfield.

109
00:06:35.927 --> 00:06:40.788
I carried a small parcel containing only some clothing, a locket, and a ring.

110
00:06:42.056 --> 00:06:43.777
My purse held twenty shillings.

111
00:06:45.098 --> 00:06:48.320
I was weeping wildly as I walked along my solitary way.

112
00:06:49.521 --> 00:06:54.044
At any moment I could have turned back and been welcomed by my master, but I pressed on.

113
00:06:55.185 --> 00:06:58.768
When I heard a coach approaching, I turned and signaled it to stop.

114
00:06:59.968 --> 00:07:05.312
I asked the driver where he was going, and he named a faraway place where I was sure

115
00:07:05.392 --> 00:07:07.393
Mr. Rochester had no connections.

116
00:07:08.614 --> 00:07:14.236
The fare would cost every shilling I had, but I climbed aboard, and the coach rolled away.
